[0,"o","\r\u001b[1;34m\u001b[0m                                                                                                                        \u001b[1;34m########################################################################################################################\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m    Exercise: Repair a File System at Boot\u001b[0m                                                                              \u001b[1;34m        Requirements\u001b[0m                                                                                                    \u001b[1;34m          Host: servera, with its VM console open\u001b[0m                                                                       \u001b[1;34m          Break the /boot entry in /etc/fstab, then repair it from the emergency shell\u001b[0m                                  \u001b[1;34m        Steps\u001b[0m                                                                                                           "]
[0.000018,"o","\u001b[1;34m          1. Break the UUID of the /boot entry in /etc/fstab\u001b[0m"]
[0.000022,"o","                                                            "]
[0.000018,"o","\u001b[1;34m          2. Reboot and log in to the emergency shell as root\u001b[0m"]
[0.00003,"o","                                                           "]
[0.000009,"o","\u001b[1;34m          3. Check that the root file system is read/write\u001b[0m"]
[0.000033,"o","                                                              \u001b[1;34m          4. Find the bad entry with mount --all\u001b[0m"]
[0.000034,"o","                                                                        "]
[0.000016,"o","\u001b[1;34m          5. Correct the entry in /etc/fstab\u001b[0m"]
[0.00002,"o","                                                                            "]
[0.000018,"o","\u001b[1;34m          6. Reload systemd and confirm mount --all succeeds\u001b[0m"]
[0.000013,"o","                                                            "]
[0.000112,"o","\u001b[1;34m          7. Reboot and confirm a normal boot\u001b[0m                                                                           \u001b[1;34m########################################################################################################################\u001b[0m"]
